the avengers have assembled and the game  lets you play as kamala khan  the hulk iron man black widow thor and  captain america  but who should you choose we're here to  help you decide by breaking down  each hero's fighting style kamala khan  aka miss marvel is the first hero you'll  spend time with in the campaign  and she's the most well-rounded of the  bunch kamala is a formidable fighter  both up close  and at range her super-sized punches are  great for getting up close and personal  and her special attacks like hi5 offer  solid crowd control  knocking enemies back at a distance she  can sling a stretchy arm at enemies in  the air  an attack you can spam without fear of  running out of ammo  or charge what's more kamala's polymorph  ability  automatically dodges enemy attacks as  she stretches around their punches and  lasers  her ultimate and biggin transforms her  into a giant even stretchier version of  herself  letting you turn the tables on all those  bad guys finally she can heal herself  and nearby allies  if you want a well-balanced hero you can  pick up easily  kamala is your girl this probably comes  as no surprise but hulk is the avengers  most  in your face fighter he might move the  slowest but he makes up for it with very  powerful melee strikes  hulk can instantly take one standard  enemy out of the fight by picking them  up and using them as a living weapon  loki's style his special attacks are  great for crowd control  thunderclap in particular is a useful  way to clear out a gang of enemies in  front of you  hulk's rage ability lets you stay in the  fight longer as you deal rage damage you  actually recover  health if you want to charge into battle  and not stop throwing punches until it's  over  hulk is for you hulk smash and you can  too  iron man is basically the polar opposite  of the hulk tony stark prefers to hover  above the action and rain down repulsor  beams from above  his moveset is very technical making him  one of the more advanced characters to  master  you'll need to recharge your long range  beams by throwing punches  so expect to do a lot of dodging and  countering while you're on the ground  from the air he can control the  battlefield with his unibeam  melting down the heavier enemies his arc  overload ability also lets him fire from  above without having to land and  recharge  if you want to stay in the sky and  support your teammates iron man is the  one to pick  black widow is the fastest hero on the  team and probably the best option for  one-on-one fights  her ultimate called power surge gives  her charged up batons to beat down ames  robots and mass  but for the most part she focuses on  grappling them one by one  she quite literally carries a grappling  hook which you can use to interrupt  enemy attacks and get right up in their  face  her abilities let her stun a target or  go invisible letting you weave in and  out of the crowd as you pick your target  if you want to focus on individual bad  guys rather than an overall view of the  battlefield  black widow is a good bite  time for a prison break just as iron man  is a technical character to play  thor's combination of flight hammer hits  and mighty magic  also makes him a tricky one to master  but where iron man dives into the battle  to take a break from firing above  thor is more suited to charging straight  into the fight taking to the skies when  you need a breather  even his ultimate which teleports him  through the bifrost is designed to give  you a break as you decide where on the  battlefield he reappears in a burst of  norse energy  mjolnir deals heavy damage to your foes  whether you're up in their face or  throwing it from afar  and thor's abilities unleash bursts of  energy that can damage whole groups of  bad dudes  thor can also activate odin force to  keep himself from taking damage while he  attacks with lightning-charged attacks  thor is a well-balanced fighter with  melee ranged and aerial options  just be prepared for some more technical  play finally there's captain america  he's the leader of the group and as such  his abilities can help support the rest  of the team in combat  his rally cry lowers enemy defenses  letting your squad deal extra damage to  anyone who gets marked  steamroller meanwhile stuns enemies as  your shield bounces all around and  strikes targets  of course steve can also pummel his  enemies with punches or throw his mighty  shield from afar  his ultimate will also get him nice and  buffed for some melee combat  if you want to help the team deal damage  while throwing some solid punches  yourself  cap is your man so hopefully this video  helps you decide which hero is right for  you  all six of the avengers have very  different play styles but that's exactly  why they work as a team  spider-man hawkeye and kate bishop are  on the way too so expect them to mix up  the dynamics even more  stay tuned to gamespot for more avengers  coverage including our full review  coming soon  [Music]  you
 

